# Catalog and documentation

If it is not in `catalog.yaml`, it is not in the book. Topics are the controlled list in that file.

- Same change as the code: leaf `README.md` (what, when, build, see-also) and a `docs/` page.
- Include source; do not duplicate it:

  ````markdown
  ```{literalinclude} ../../../path/to/main.cpp
  :language: cpp
  :start-after: // start the-id
  :end-before: // end the-id
  ```
  ````

- `status: complete` only when code, README, catalog row, and docs page all exist. `planned` is backlog (no folder required). Avoid merging `draft`.
- Exercises: spoilers stay out of `prompt.md`. Solutions are a Sphinx dropdown (HTML) and a PDF appendix, never HTML-only.
- Voice: engineering/scientific. Math is welcome. CS jargon needs an engineering consequence.
- Skill `write-scientific-docs` for page shape; skill `review-catalog-entry` before you call it done.
